<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! face.circle.unfollows ~ the unfollow: a nym leaves a circle

`lares circle remove <nym> --to <circle>` drops the nym from the circle. The handle-book's memory of it stays; nothing crosses the wire.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/shows`>>

!! shows ~ unfollow

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`example` name=`unfollow` params=`nym/<nym> ~ drop the nym from following`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/takes`>>

!! takes ~ nym · to · face

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`arg` name=`nym` params=`takes/nym needs/required seat/1 as/<nym> ~ the nym's verifying key, hex`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`to` params=`takes/circle default/following ~ the circle; following, the primary system circle, stands by default`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`face` params=`takes/index ~ the face whose handle-book and circles act; absent, the one face standing open`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/gate`>>

!! gate ~ local

Testimony: the door checks; this slot grants nothing.

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`gate` name=`local` params=`who/seat-or-hand ~ edits this face's private graph alone; nothing crosses the wire`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

